  "summary": "I worked all 8 original results-inbox items and 4 that arrived while I was working (RBC-INBOX-01). One item is still open on purpose. Two of the new arrivals changed decisions I had already made, so I corrected those.\n\n**Patients needing action**\n- **Raj Patel (pt-0006), CT urogram 10/19:** No mass or stone to explain the hematuria. A 4 mm LLL nodule is already followed in lung cancer screening.\n  - First I ordered a 12-month screening low-dose CT (sr-t0001). Then a Lakeshore addendum to his 4/14 screening CT arrived: a new 5 mm RUL nodule, Lung-RADS 3, repeat CT in 6 months.\n  - Corrected: new low-dose CT ordered for 10/23–11/14 (sr-t0032), with a tracking task due 11/14. I sent him a corrected message, wrote notes, and closed both items.\n  - **I couldn't cancel sr-t0001 or its tracking task (task-t0002) — I have no tool for that.** I asked scheduling (task-t0034) not to book it and to discontinue both. Please confirm that's done.\n  - The urology/cystoscopy decision for the hematuria is yours; I deferred it in the note.\n- **Leslie Parisian (pt-0007):**\n  - ED CTA, preliminary read: the final report says the \"RUL nodule\" is a vessel, no PE, no lung follow-up needed. Closed with that comment.\n  - BMP 10/22: creatinine went from 0.98 to 1.64 within 35 hours, which counts as kidney injury (AKI). He is on ibuprofen from the ED and naproxen as needed.\n  - I ordered an urgent repeat BMP by Monday 10/26, sent him an urgent message (stop NSAIDs), created an RN triage call task due 10/26, and wrote a note.\n  - **I also put his naproxen order on hold.** Policy doesn't require this; I did it because of the kidney injury. Please review.\n- **Walter Brennan (pt-0008), potassium 6.4:** At first it was flagged hemolyzed (possibly falsely high), so I ordered an urgent repeat BMP and messaged him to come in by Monday.\n  - The lab then corrected it: not hemolyzed, so the 6.4 stands. Corrected: on-call notified at stat priority, stat BMP ordered for today (replaces the urgent order sr-t0018), corrected message telling him to come in today, stat RN call task.\n  - His medication review found nothing that clearly raises potassium. He's on metoprolol, which can modestly; I left it unchanged because stopping it abruptly isn't safe with his heart disease, and flagged it to on-call. Notes written.\n- **Carol Whitfield (pt-0033):**\n  - BMP creatinine 1.31: the 10/21 value of 0.84 was entered in error, so I didn't compare against it. Against her valid 1.27 from 10/17 it isn't kidney injury; closed with no action.\n  - Then an urgent care creatinine of 1.78 arrived, collected the same evening — a rise of 0.47 within 48 hours, which is kidney injury. Urgent repeat BMP by 10/26, urgent message to her, note written. Her HCTZ (started 10/17) is flagged for your review.\n\n**Closed with no action**\n- **Edra Ondricka (pt-0016):** TSH 2.1 is normal. The potassium was corrected from 6.3 (analyzer fault) to 4.4, also normal.\n\n**Misfiled fax**\n- **pt-0065:** The Lakeshore addendum (Lung-RADS 4A, new 8 mm nodule) is for a Judith Nowicki with a different date of birth and MRN. No Riverbend patient matches.\n  - I placed no orders and didn't contact our patient. An urgent RN triage task (task-t0015) asks them to tell Lakeshore so the finding reaches the right patient's clinician, and to have the fax removed from her chart.\n\n**Left open**\n- **inbox-a0002, Parisian chest X-ray 10/22:** Only a preliminary read exists (possible 7 mm RUL opacity, \"consider CT chest\"). Per policy it stays open until the final report is issued.\n\nYour messages queue has 6 refill requests from before I started; I didn't work them because this task covered the results inbox.",
